This doesn't sound good - for the short term it is good. However, this is very childish behavior, and very dependent behavior. In the end, you won't feel like a King, but you'll feel you're living with an echo. 

I'd recommend you discuss this with her. Instill in her that is it perfectly ok to have her own opinions and disagree with you. Try to engage in debates. She cannot be dependent on you else this will become tiring. We're meant to fall in love with other people, not ourselves. 

&amp;#x200B;

This is a few months into a relationship - this is her. She wouldn't have changed that fast, nor got comfortable. It sounds like you just see potential in her and don't actually find her that appealing.

If you've only been dating a few months, I doubt you're even in love yet - and if you're already calling her out for what she's wearing, I'd say it's unlikely you ever will be with this girl.

&amp;#x200B;
